into Steven Wright jokes.

17:34.657 --> 17:37.750
<i>I spilled spot remover on my dog.
Now he's gone.</i>

17:37.860 --> 17:39.020
Oh, this is bogus!

17:42.964 --> 17:44.956
Two shakes, that's it. Move along.

17:45.066 --> 17:47.433
Oh. Why, thank you, tinkle fairy.

17:49.506 --> 17:51.494
Lois, you ruined everything,
you know that?

17:51.607 --> 17:55.042
Peter, I know it's a little extreme.
But when it comes to our children,

17:55.142 --> 17:57.704
it's better to err on the safe side.
Isn't that right?

17:57.812 --> 18:00.872
No. You know, Lois,
if everybody was as closed-minded as you,

18:00.982 --> 18:03.850
the world wouldn't have
some of its most inspired creations.

18:05.454 --> 18:08.547
Man, this chocolate bar is delicious.

18:10.259 --> 18:12.988
Oh, yeah. I love peanut butter.

18:17.298 --> 18:19.358
I'm Officer Reeses. What happened here?

18:19.467 --> 18:21.992
He got peanut butter on my chocolate.

18:22.103 --> 18:24.731
He got chocolate in my peanut butter.

18:31.480 --> 18:33.038
Oh, come on.

18:33.147 --> 18:35.172
I know what'll make you feel better.

18:35.283 --> 18:38.344
- How about a little angry sex, huh?
- Oh, all right.

18:39.521 --> 18:42.421
Whoa! Whoa!
Those actions are highly inappropriate.

18:42.522 --> 18:45.014
What? Wait a minute.
We're not allowed to have sex?

18:45.126 --> 18:46.219
Oh, you can have sex.

18:46.327 --> 18:50.731
Just no moaning, no tongue-kissing,
no thrusting, no movement whatsoever.

18:54.236 --> 18:57.033
Well, this isn't very romantic.
I mean, how are we supposed to...

18:57.139 --> 18:58.731
I'm done. Night, Lois.

19:04.679 --> 19:06.374
Come on, you son of a...

19:07.916 --> 19:09.749
Oh... me.

19:09.852 --> 19:12.183
- Brian, would you mind?
- Yeah, sure.

19:12.287 --> 19:13.549
Oh, sorry.

19:13.655 --> 19:17.318
I haven't had sex in two weeks.
I'm just a little on edge lately.

19:17.659 --> 19:20.786
A little? There wasn't this much tension
when the slaves were freed.

19:20.895 --> 19:23.329
Okay, so you're free to go.

19:24.032 --> 19:25.397
But we're cool, right?

19:25.800 --> 19:27.267
Peter, we have to talk.

19:27.368 --> 19:30.099
Look, I thought this FCC thing
was a good idea at first,

19:30.204 --> 19:31.934
but it's just gone way too far.

19:32.040 --> 19:34.601
- What are you saying, Lois?
- Well,

19:35.277 --> 19:37.836
I don't want to admit it,
but I think you were right.

19:37.946 --> 19:40.575
I don't believe it! Finally I can do this!

19:42.817 --> 19:46.308
I set that thing up 15 years ago.
Hey, where's the clown?

19:46.421 --> 19:49.822
We've got to do something about this.
Pack your bag, Peter.

19:49.924 --> 19:51.618
We're going to Washington.

19:52.227 --> 19:53.319
Oh, there he is.

19:55.363 --> 19:57.730
- Are we there yet?
- No, Chris, honey, we're not.

19:57.831 --> 19:59.891
- Are we there yet?
- No, Chris.

20:00.000 --> 20:02.765
- Are we there yet?
- Yes, Chris, yes. Okay? We're there.

20:02.870 --> 20:03.894
Liar!

20:04.005 --> 20:08.500
<i>East of Eden? So you pretty much do
whatever Oprah tells you to, huh?</i>

20:08.610 --> 20:11.579
You know, this book's been around
for 50 years. It's a classic.

20:11.679 --> 20:13.010
But you just got it last week,

20:13.114 --> 20:15.082
and there's a giant Oprah sticker
on the front.

20:15.183 --> 20:17.742
Is that what that is?
Let me just peel that right off.

20:17.852 --> 20:19.616
So, what are you gonna read
after that one?

20:19.721 --> 20:21.086
Well, she hasn't told us yet. Damn!

20:24.026 --> 20:27.927
<i>And the motion carries.
The janitor's new nickname is Sweepy.</i>

20:38.539 --> 20:40.871
Gentlemen, that was a fart.

20:40.975 --> 20:43.670
- What's going on out here?
- I'll tell you what's going on.

20:43.778 --> 20:47.680
This government's FCC is trying to take
all the farts away from television!

20:47.783 --> 20:50.308
And all the sex, and all the nudity,
and all the poop.

20:50.419 --> 20:51.976
Well, I say it's wrong.

20:52.086 --> 20:54.885
These things are part of the fabric
of American life.

20:54.990 --> 20:58.754
Well, we appreciate your passion
but this Congress supports the FCC.

20:58.859 --> 21:01.521
- Indecency is un-American.
- Oh, yeah?

21:01.629 --> 21:03.927
Well, I can prove to you
that that's a bunch of bull.

21:04.032 --> 21:05.090
Look around you.

21:05.199 --> 21:09.135
The Washington Monument.
Looks an awful lot like a penis, doesn't it?

21:09.236 --> 21:12.673
The Capitol Building,
quite obviously a giant boob.

21:12.774 --> 21:14.265
And the Pentagon?

21:14.376 --> 21:18.141
Well, you look me in the eye and tell me
it doesn't look like a big anus.

21:18.246 --> 21:21.215
My God!
How could we have been so blind?

21:21.315 --> 21:22.475
He's absolutely right.

21:22.584 --> 21:26.111
Come to think of it, have you ever looked
closely at the Lincoln Memorial?

21:29.158 --> 21:33.720
<i>Our top story, the FCC's content ban
on Quahog has finally been lifted.</i>

21:33.827 --> 21:36.957
Well, you did it, Peter. You beat the FCC.

21:37.365 --> 21:40.333
<i>Lois, Lois,
let's watch The Brady Bunch.</i>

21:40.568 --> 21:42.037
Look what I did, everybody.

21:42.136 --> 21:46.004
Isn't it the biggest,
most super-special poop you've ever seen?

21:46.240 --> 21:50.699
Well, Cindy, I guess it's true
that big things come in small packages.

21:50.700 --> 22:51.700
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru